.TH NIBWARDEN\-SSH\-SIGN 1 2026-11-06 "nibwarden" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nibwarden\-ssh\-sign \- sign git commits with an SSH key from the nibwarden vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nibwarden\-ssh\-sign
.I ssh\-keygen\-arguments
.SH DESCRIPTION
git runs
.B nibwarden\-ssh\-sign
as its
.B gpg.ssh.program
after
.BR "nibwarden ssh git\-setup" .
It runs
.BR ssh\-keygen (1)
with the same arguments, pointed at nibwarden's SSH agent, whatever agent the rest of
the session uses.
.PP
Before signing it makes sure the vault is unlocked, asking for the master password
on the terminal when there is one; every signature is approved in a window
(or, without one, after
.BR "nibwarden ssh authorize" ).
Verifying needs no vault.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nibwarden (1),
.BR ssh\-keygen (1),
.BR git\-config (1)
